    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the offensive unit. **Gunnar Henderson** carries the highest score of the day at 76.04; despite facing a high-caliber arm in Cole, the park factors and **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s elite base projections make him a must-start staple in the #3 hole. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Bradish, with his 74.56 efficiency score bolstered by a 16% park adjustment and an advantageous dynamic platoon pairing that offsets his opponent\u2019s skill level. **Heliot Ramos** also presents a strong play (67.47) in the same contest, though we remain mindful that the high-efficiency environment is tempered slightly by the need to balance our SB-scarcity goals against the opposing battery's defensive aptitude.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Nasim Nunez**, who fell just short of our 40-point threshold with a score of 39.47. While **Nasim Nunez** provides the elite sprint speed profile we typically aggressively target to secure our category leads, his matchup against deGrom proved too daunting; the expected SP skill penalty outweighed the utility of his speed, forcing us to prioritize the higher floor offered by **Miguel Vargas** and **Drake Baldwin**. Regarding the rest of the roster, we continue to monitor the status of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who remains on the IL, while **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Andy Pages** are excluded today due to team off-days. With **Drake Baldwin** (65.45) and **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) providing solid value in the top-third of the order, we are well-positioned to chase volume, provided our lower-order bats like **Luis Lara** (41.15) can avoid empty plate appearances against a tough Kirby outing.",
